      "hints": [
        "Expand LHS: $\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta$.",
        "Group as $\\sin\\theta(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(1 - \\sin^2\\theta)$.",
        "Use $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ to reach $\\sin^3\\theta + \\cos^3\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand the brackets on the left-hand side:\n$$\\text{LHS} = (\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta)(1 - \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta) = \\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta\\cos^2\\theta$$",
        "Group terms with common factors of $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\sin\\theta(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(1 - \\sin^2\\theta)$$",
        "Apply the Pythagorean identities $1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$ and $1 - \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\sin\\theta(\\sin^2\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(\\cos^2\\theta) = \\sin^3\\theta + \\cos^3\\theta = \\text{RHS}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Identities": "Expands product (M1). Groups and applies identities (M1). Obtains $\\sin^3\\theta + \\cos^3\\theta$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
