      "hints": [
        "Use identity from (i): $\\sin^3\\theta + \\cos^3\\theta = 3\\cos^3\\theta \\implies \\sin^3\\theta = 2\\cos^3\\theta$.",
        "Divide by $\\cos^3\\theta \\implies \\tan^3\\theta = 2 \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\sqrt[3]{2}$.",
        "Solve for $\\theta = 51.6^\\circ, 231.6^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the identity from part (i) into the equation:\n$$\\sin^3\\theta + \\cos^3\\theta = 3\\cos^3\\theta \\implies \\sin^3\\theta = 2\\cos^3\\theta$$",
        "Divide both sides by $\\cos^3\\theta$ and take the cube root:\n$$\\tan^3\\theta = 2 \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\sqrt[3]{2} \\approx 1.2599$$",
        "Find all solutions for $\\theta$ in the range $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 360^\\circ$ (to 1 decimal place):\n$$\\theta_1 = \\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt[3]{2}) \\approx 51.56^\\circ \\approx 51.6^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta_2 = 180^\\circ + 51.56^\\circ = 231.56^\\circ \\approx 231.6^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 51.6^\\circ, \\quad 231.6^\\circ$$"
      ],
